/*
  MageRide Driver — iOS · C087 driver-ios-vehicle-onboarding. English, the development region.

  SCOPE. Cluster 2 only: SCR-DI-004…004c the Mode-C wizard, SCR-DI-005 the document scanner,
  SCR-DI-006 the verdict list, SCR-DI-026/026a My Vehicles.

  KEYS ARE C069'S. Same key names and the same translations as
  `apps/driver-android/src/main/res/values*/strings.xml`, so a divergence between the two driver
  apps is a diff rather than an archaeology exercise.

  FORMAT SPECIFIERS ARE NOT. Android writes `%1$s` for a string argument; `String(format:)` reads
  `%s` as a C string and would print rubbish, so every one of them is `%1$@` here. `%1$d` is the
  same on both. `LocalizationTests` asserts each specifier survives into si and ta.

  FOUR ANDROID KEYS ARE ABSENT, and each one is a control iOS draws for us. `capture_flash`,
  `capture_retake` and `capture_use_photo` are VNDocumentCameraViewController's own buttons — it
  localises them itself, in the driver's language — and `capture_target_delivery_proof` belongs to
  the delivery cluster, which is C089's on this platform. A key with no renderer is a translation
  nobody can check.

  TWO KEYS ARE NEW HERE. `vehicles_select` and `vehicles_swipe_hint` are the wireframe's own iOS
  copy: `driver_ios.html` labels an eligible row `Select ›` and puts deactivate on `.swipeActions`,
  where Android draws a `Remove` text button that needs no announcing.
*/

